.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
. * I refrain from using the alternative specification using a 2SLS IV-regressi
> on, as I have serious concerns about the exclusion restriction being violated
> . Thus, I stick with the main specification: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Having Daughters (Daughters) leads to higher actual Gender Equality
>  (ActualGE).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with ActualGE 
> as dependent variable and the dummy variable Daughters as independent variabl
> e, additionally controlling for total number of children (sumkids), income (h
> ghinc), education (pgbilzeit), marital status (partner), migration background
>  (migback), male (male) using heteroskedasticity robus standard errors
. 
.         regress ActualGE Daughters sumkids hghinc pgbilzeit ib1.partner ib1.m
> igback i.male, robust

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        813
                                                F(9, 803)         =      10.53
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0000
                                                R-squared         =     0.0844
                                                Root MSE          =      4.613

